implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review of your own diff (load the adversarial-self-review skill). git diff in the worktree must show exactly the two paths. Check:
(a) the gate sits before state.getTask and before every transition, approval and WIP check, and nothing above it writes;
(b) an absent key is allowed; '', null, a non-string and an unregistered unprefixed id are refused; the team role wins over the id prefix (workerHasRole and resolveWorkerRole are unchanged), so a governor-prefixed id on a worker team is refused, as in the sibling gates;
(c) concurrency: the handler runs under the global state mutex and the gate only reads team membership, so no write can slip past it between two calls;
(d) every in-repo caller still works: the only test caller passing a workerId is activityActor.test.ts (governor-z, allowed); scripts/tests/onboarding.mjs:200 and wave1-pilot.mjs:490 strip MOE_* before they spawn the proxy; src/benchmarks/baselineRun.ts calls through scripts/moe-call.sh outside a seat; the governor prompts in moe-agent.{sh,ps1} keep working for governor seats;
(e) no added line contains a project.json globalRails.forbiddenPatterns string;
(f) the refusal and the description point only at a route a refused seat can use: chat_send is open to every role (TOOL_AUDIENCE ALL; mem:gotcha-role-aware-refusals-tools-list).
Fix anything found in the same two files, then rerun checkRef #1 and use that fresh run as the complete_task verification.
